==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*dewk-}}
{{inh+|en|enm|induction}}, from {{der|en|fro|induction}}, from {{der|en|la|inductiō}}, from {{m|la|indūcō|t=I lead}}. {{surf|en|induct|-ion}} or {{af|en|induce|-tion}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ɪnˈdʌkʃən/}}
* {{rhymes|en|ʌkʃən|s=3}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-induction.wav |Audio (UK)}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# An act of [[induct]]ing.
#* {{RQ:Beaumont Fletcher Comedies and Tragedies|The Honest Man's Fortune|2|1|passage=I know not you; nor am I well pleased to make this time, as the affair now stands, the '''induction''' of your acquaintance.}}
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Henry 4-1|III|i|passage=These promises are fair, the parties sure, / And our '''induction''' full of prosperous hope.}}
## A [[formal]] [[ceremony]] in which a person is appointed to an [[office]] or into [[military]] [[service]].
## The process of showing a newcomer around a place where they will work or study.
# An act of [[induce|inducing]].
#* {{quote-book|en|passage=One of the first examples of the immunogenicity of recombinantly derived antibodies was with murine anti-CD3 monoclonal antibody (OKT3) used in the '''induction''' of immunosupression after organ transplantation.| page=699| title=Modern Pharmaceutics| edition=4th| author=Gilbert S. Banker & Christopher T. Rhodes| publisher=Informa Health Care| year=2002| isbn=0824706749}}
## {{lb|en|physics}} [[generation|Generation]] of an [[electric]] [[current]] by a [[varying]] [[magnetic]] [[field]].
## {{lb|en|logic}} [[derivation|Derivation]] of [[general]] [[principle]]s from [[specific]] [[instance]]s.
## {{lb|en|mathematics}} A method of [[proof]] of a [[theorem]] by first proving it for a specific case (often an [[integer]]; usually 0 or 1) and showing that, if it is true for one case then it must be true for the next.
## {{lb|en|theater}} Use of rumors to twist and [[complicate]] the plot of a play or to [[narrate]] in a way that does not have to state truth nor fact within the play.
## {{lb|en|embryology}} Given a group of [[cell]]s that emits or displays a substance, the influence of this substance on the [[fate]] of a second group of cells
## {{lb|en|mechanical engineering}} The delivery of [[air]] to the [[cylinder]]s of an [[internal combustion]] [[piston engine]].
# {{lb|en|medicine}} The process of [[inducing]] the birth process.
# {{lb|en|obsolete}} An [[introduction]].
#* {{RQ:Massinger The Fatal Dowry}}
#*: This is but an '''induction''': I'lldraw / The curtains of the tragedy hereafter.

